#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:2
msgid "Building snap rpms on RHEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:4
msgid ""
"Snap is  currently available for  [Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) 8]"
"(https://www.redhat.com/en/enterprise-linux-8) and RHEL 7.6+. See {ref}"
"`Installing snap on Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) <interfaces-installing-"
"snap-on-red-hat>` for installation instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:6
msgid ""
"However, if you are an advanced user and wish to see how *snap* is built, "
"its RPMs can be built and manually installed relatively easily, as outlined "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:8
msgid "Building the RPM manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:10
msgid ""
"First, both the new developer-centric [CodeReady Linux Builder](https://"
"developers.redhat.com/blog/2018/11/15/introducing-codeready-linux-builder/) "
"and the [AppStream](https://developers.redhat.com/blog/2018/11/15/rhel8-"
"introducing-appstreams/) additional user space application repositories need "
"to be added, followed by the [Extra Packages for Enterprise Linux](https://"
"fedoraproject.org/wiki/EPEL) repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:12
msgid ""
"$ sudo subscription-manager repos --enable codeready-builder-for-rhel-8-"
"x86_64-rpms\n"
"$ sudo subscription-manager repos --enable rhel-8-for-x86_64-appstream-rpms\n"
"$ sudo dnf install https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/epel-release-"
"latest-8.noarch.rpm\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:18
msgid "Next, refresh the package list and install a few dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:20
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf upgrade\n"
"$ sudo dnf module install go-toolset\n"
"$ sudo dnf install rpmdevtools\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:26
msgid ""
"The snapd code base includes an [RPM SPEC file](https://rpm-packaging-"
"guide.github.io/#what-is-a-spec-file), which [contains the recipe](https://"
"github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/2.42/packaging/fedora/snapd.spec) used to "
"build the RPM packages. To setup the RPM build environment, first prepare "
"the RPM tree in your home directory, fetch the source tarballs and extract "
"the RPM spec:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:28
msgid ""
"$ rpmdev-setuptree\n"
"$ cd ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES\n"
"$ curl -L \\\n"
"    https://github.com/canonical/snapd/releases/download/2.42/snapd_2.42.no-"
"vendor.tar.xz \\\n"
"    -o snapd_2.42.no-vendor.tar.xz\n"
"$ tar -xvJ -C ~/rpmbuild/SPECS --strip-components=3 \\\n"
"    -f snapd_2.42.no-vendor.tar.xz \\\n"
"    snapd-2.42/packaging/fedora/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:39
msgid ""
"Then, while still in `~/rpmbuild/SOURCES`, fetch the remaining release "
"packages and install the build dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:41
msgid ""
"$ spectool -g ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/snapd.spec\n"
"$ sudo dnf builddep ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/snapd.spec -y\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:46
msgid ""
"Three RPMs form the complete snapd installation, and these are built as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:48
msgid "$ rpmbuild -bb ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/snapd.spec\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:52
msgid "Finally, all three RPM packages can be installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:54
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf localinstall \\\n"
"   ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/snap-confine-2.42-0.el8.x86_64.rpm \\\n"
"   ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/snapd-2.42-0.el8.x86_64.rpm \\\n"
"   ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/noarch/snapd-selinux-2.42-0.el8.noarch.rpm\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:61
msgid ""
"Once installed, the *systemd* unit that manages the main snap communication "
"socket needs to be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:63
msgid "$ sudo systemctl enable --now snapd.socket\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:67
msgid ""
"The snapd environment can now be tested, and hopefully, used productively:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:69
msgid "$ snap install hello-world\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/building-snap-rpms-on-rhel.md:72
msgid "A reboot/logout/login should put hello-world in the path."
msgstr ""
